senses.gloss:
(I)--a name of the sun;
1: Br. II. १३. १२५.
garden of, in the north;
2: वा. ३६. ११; १०३. ५९.
protects the यमुना;
3: M. २५३. ३०, ४२.
has seven horses as वाहनस्;
4: Ib. १०४. 8.
wor- shipped on the eve of palace building.
5: Ib. १२८. ३६; २६८. २१.

(IV)--the विष्कम्ब of the sun; is 9,००० yojanas; thrice is the मण्डल in measurement;
1: वा. ५३. ५४, ६१.
of वैशाख in the चाक्षुष epoch; the first planet of all;
2: Ib. ५३. १०४.
brought forth with [page३-568+ ३०] श्रवण and placed in Dhruva;
3: Ib. ५३. १११.
in the shape of a circle; the lord of the world.
4: Ib. ५३. ११८.

--a son of Aditi, married पृष्णि in the Vaivas- vata and became father of सावित्रि and others. Fought with Virocana in a देवासुर war; आदित्य of the month आषाढ; the fifth व्यास; milkman of gods on the earth;
2: Br. II. २४. ३४ and ३९; ३५. ११८; ३६. २०६; III. २४. ७८; ५७. २२.
heard the पुराण from बृहस्पति and narrated it to मृत्यु. ^1 भा. VI. 6. ३९; १८. 1; VIII. १०. २९; X. ५८. २०; XII. 6. ६८: Br. II. २३. २४; २४. ७६ and ९९; III. 7. २८८ and ९३. वा. ५३. ७९. ^3 Br. IV. 4. ५९-60; २४. ५९.

(IV)--ब्रह्मा contemplated her in his mind when engaged in creation; at that time a being half male and half female broke through his body and it was named शतरूपा;
1: M. 3. ३०.
also called सरस्वती, गायत्री and ब्रह्माणी;
2: Ib. 4. १०; १८७. ४५; २६०. ४४.
विश्वरूपा with two feet; came out by cutting through the head of ब्रह्मा.
3: वा. २३. ७८, ९१.

(I)--s.v. 8th Manu of the future;
1: भा. V. १९. १०.
अश्वत्थामन् and others are sages; he would have ten sons like धृति, वरीयन् etc;
2: M. 9. ३१.
a son of विवस्वान्; engaged in penance in Meru;
3: Ib. ११. 9, ३८.
शुक्र Predicted Bali, a grandson of प्रह्लाद as king in सवर्णि's Kingdom.
4: Ib. ४७. २१८; २४७. ७२;
